WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.204 --> 00:00:01.310
(bells ringing)

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.803
- People assume that to
ring a bell at the church

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:06.552
it’s just by pulling one rope and one bell.

00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:08.885
But our church is different.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.552
It's not as easy as it looks.

00:00:13.552 --> 00:00:16.219
It does feel like a dance to me.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.592
My name is Okalena
Patricia Lekanoff Gregory,

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.307
and I play the bells at the
Holy Ascension Cathedral

00:00:29.307 --> 00:00:31.530
here in Unalaska.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.994
Unalaska Island is located
out in the Aleutian chain

00:00:34.994 --> 00:00:38.324
in between the Pacific
Ocean and the Bering Sea.

00:00:38.324 --> 00:00:40.740
The church is a very iconic place,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.907
and wherever you go on this
island, you could see it.

00:00:50.724 --> 00:00:54.616
I've been ringing the
bells maybe 35 years.

00:00:54.616 --> 00:00:55.449
To ring the bells,

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:58.282
we go up a flight of steep stairs.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.317
Step up onto the platform.

00:01:06.397 --> 00:01:10.086
And then you put your right
foot on the one big bell.

00:01:10.086 --> 00:01:12.535
Your left foot on the other big bell.

00:01:12.535 --> 00:01:14.210
And then the smaller bells,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.221
you twist your hands and then pull 'em.

00:01:16.221 --> 00:01:19.537
(bells clanging)

00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:21.289
There are only a handful of other people

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:22.941
that know how to ring the bells.

00:01:22.941 --> 00:01:24.437
There is no written music.

00:01:24.437 --> 00:01:27.309
I just have to play them
by what I was taught

00:01:27.309 --> 00:01:28.924
from watching my dad.

00:01:28.924 --> 00:01:32.499
My dad has been playing
the bells for 60 years.

00:01:32.499 --> 00:01:33.946
He learned from his godfather.

00:01:33.946 --> 00:01:35.315
I'm teaching my daughter

00:01:35.315 --> 00:01:37.815
and then also my great-nieces.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:41.478
For me to learn to ring the bells

00:01:41.478 --> 00:01:44.107
and to pass on my dad's legacy,

00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:46.791
I think is real important.

00:01:46.791 --> 00:01:48.955
It's an honor, of course,
to be ringing the bells

00:01:48.955 --> 00:01:50.683
because you're ringing it for God to hear

00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:52.102
and for the people to hear.

00:01:52.102 --> 00:01:54.352
And that's important to me.

